From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <d.darrigo@outlook.it>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] soc/intel/cannonlake: A firmware watchdog from the option
 firmware_watchdog

SOC_INTEL_CANNONLAKE_FIRMWARE_WATCHDOG, for a board to select: romstage
arms the overclocking watchdog of the PCH before the memory init, with
the timeout of the option "firmware_watchdog" (seconds, 0 for off,
never below 180), ramstage reloads it at the payload and logs what is
left of OC_WDT_CTL after FSP-S, and the SMI handler stops it when the
payload confirms the RW slot (SMMSTORE_CMD_VBOOT_SLOT_GOOD, through a
weak smmstore_firmware_confirmed()). A boot that hangs in between is
reset by the PCH, so that a new slot on trial falls back after two
hangs without anyone at the power button. Off, and on S3 resume, where
the payload does not run, romstage stops the watchdog whatever a
previous firmware left, and it logs a reset that came from it.

Read on a Lenovo ThinkCentre M920x (Cannon Point-H) under the Coffee
Lake FSP 7.0.74.20: OC_WDT_CTL 0x00002000 at the OS, the watchdog there
and off, left alone by FSP-M and FSP-S. The armed path is not tested
on a machine yet.
---
 src/drivers/smmstore/smi.c                    |  8 +++
 src/include/smmstore.h                        |  3 +
 src/soc/intel/cannonlake/Kconfig              | 12 ++++
 src/soc/intel/cannonlake/Makefile.mk          |  3 +
 src/soc/intel/cannonlake/firmware_watchdog.c  | 69 +++++++++++++++++++
 .../include/soc/firmware_watchdog.h           | 14 ++++
 src/soc/intel/cannonlake/romstage/romstage.c  |  2 +
 7 files changed, 111 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 src/soc/intel/cannonlake/firmware_watchdog.c
 create mode 100644 src/soc/intel/cannonlake/include/soc/firmware_watchdog.h

diff --git a/src/drivers/smmstore/smi.c b/src/drivers/smmstore/smi.c
index 6b99d7b5517..c48a16ae242 100644
--- a/src/drivers/smmstore/smi.c
+++ b/src/drivers/smmstore/smi.c
@@ -12,6 +12,7 @@
 #include <stddef.h>
 #include <stdint.h>
 #include <string.h>
+#include <types.h>
 #include <version.h>
 
 /*
@@ -282,6 +283,12 @@ static uint32_t vboot_try_other(void)
 	return SMMSTORE_RET_SUCCESS;
 }
 
+/*
+ * The payload confirmed the RW slot (SMMSTORE_CMD_VBOOT_SLOT_GOOD): the
+ * firmware booted. A platform with a firmware watchdog stops it here.
+ */
+__weak void smmstore_firmware_confirmed(void) {}
+
 uint32_t smmstore_exec(uint8_t command, void *param)
 {
 	uint32_t ret = SMMSTORE_RET_FAILURE;
@@ -353,6 +360,7 @@ uint32_t smmstore_exec(uint8_t command, void *param)
 			break;
 		}
 		vbnv_mark_tried_slot_good();
+		smmstore_firmware_confirmed();
 		ret = SMMSTORE_RET_SUCCESS;
 		break;
 	case SMMSTORE_CMD_VBOOT_TRY_OTHER:
diff --git a/src/include/smmstore.h b/src/include/smmstore.h
index a10ca44cbcb..563533ae180 100644
--- a/src/include/smmstore.h
+++ b/src/include/smmstore.h
@@ -219,4 +219,7 @@ bool smmstore_options_write_allowed(size_t offset, const void *data, size_t size
 struct lb_header;
 void lb_smmstorev2(struct lb_header *header);
 
+/* Called by the SMI handler when the payload confirms the RW slot (weak) */
+void smmstore_firmware_confirmed(void);
+
 #endif
